  <action>
    **Check A — visible independent of scroll.** Load a settings page long enough to
    scroll (assert its scroll height actually exceeds the viewport, or the check is
    vacuous). Scroll to the bottom. Commit a field. Assert the status region's own
    `getBoundingClientRect()` is within the viewport AND that the region is not covered at
    its centre point by another element (`document.elementFromPoint` resolving to the
    region or a descendant) — being on-screen but under the tab bar is the same failure as
    being scrolled past. Run at 360 px and at desktop width, in both themes.

    **Check B — every failure kind is visible.** For EACH of the four kinds, induce a
    genuine instance and assert FOUR things together as one fact ("nothing was saved, and
    the visitor can tell"):
    (i) the retry affordance is visible;
    (ii) the status region does NOT hold the saved word;
    (iii) the toast carries the EXISTING `data-quick-failed-text` string — asserted
         against the page's own attribute, never a hardcoded literal, so a second failure
         vocabulary would fail this check;
    (iv) the value is NOT on disk.
    Inducement per kind: **non-204** via a value the server's own validation rejects (the
    200-is-not-204 branch 27-04 deliberately left in place); **network error** via
    Playwright route interception aborting the request; **timeout** via route interception
    that delays the response past the bounded timeout; **opaque redirect** via an
    interception returning a cross-origin redirect (or by expiring the session, whichever
    the harness can do deterministically). If any one kind cannot be induced
    deterministically in this harness, SAY SO PLAINLY with what was tried — do not assert
    it passes by analogy with another kind.

    **Check C — the retry recovers.** Induce a failure, assert the affordance appeared,
    then REMOVE the fault and click retry. Assert the value is now ON DISK, the status
    region reaches the saved word, and the affordance is hidden again. This is the
    "recoverable" half of the only claim this phase is entitled to make, and without it
    the affordance is decoration.

    **Check D — absent otherwise.** On a clean successful save, assert the retry
    affordance is not visible at any point, and that it never became visible transiently
    (sample during the save, not only after — a control that flashes on every save is a
    permanent fixture with extra steps, which is exactly what "zero boutons" refuses).

    Add a companion source-level check in `test_companion_app.py` pinning that
    `dirty-state.js` reads the retry label from a server-rendered attribute and that all
    four failure kinds are distinguishable in its source — modelled on the existing
    `_dirty_state_script_es5_safe_reads_two_save_status_attributes()` check, which will
    itself need updating for the new attribute.

    Update `test_config_page.py`'s two existing save-status checks for the new markup
    WITHOUT weakening their contract (empty at rest, `role="status"`, `aria-live="polite"`,
    both words translated).

    MUTATION-TEST and QUOTE EVERY MESSAGE VERBATIM:
    - M-A: remove the sticky/fixed positioning. Check A must fail at 360 px, naming the
      region's off-viewport or covered position.
    - M-B: make the timeout never fire. Check B's timeout case must fail.
    - M-C: reveal the retry affordance unconditionally on every save. Check D must fail,
      and it must fail on the DURING-save sample, not only the after-save one.
    - M-D: make the retry click hide the affordance without re-attempting the save. Check
      C must fail on the on-disk clause — proving the check tests recovery rather than
      the affordance's disappearance.
    - M-E: replace the toast copy with a new literal string. Check B clause (iii) must
      fail for every kind.

    Revert every mutation with `git checkout-index -f -- <path>`, never `git checkout --`.

    Re-derive `EXPECTED_CHECK_COUNT` for every harness touched by RUNNING it.

    **THE OVERCLAIM BAN APPLIES TO CHECK NAMES AND DESCRIPTIONS.** No check may be named
